WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.745
"Do you ride with the caravan too?" asked Mandy.

2
00:00:04.746 --> 00:00:08.281
"Sometimes," replied Berk.

3
00:00:08.282 --> 00:00:12.559
"My father and I have traveled the entire empire."

4
00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:16.010
"That must be fun!" said Vinnie.

5
00:00:16.011 --> 00:00:20.544
"Most of the time, it is," Berk said, smiling.

6
00:00:20.545 --> 00:00:23.246
They arrived at a coffee shop.

7
00:00:23.247 --> 00:00:27.344
Men were outside sitting and drinking coffee.

8
00:00:27.345 --> 00:00:29.544
The children went in.

9
00:00:29.545 --> 00:00:33.209
Some men were smoking from a big pipe.

10
00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:37.670
Berk gave his father’s bag to Hasad, the shop owner.

11
00:00:37.671 --> 00:00:41.078
Hasad gave Berk a bag in return.

12
00:00:41.079 --> 00:00:44.219
Hasad spoke to Berk quietly.

13
00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:48.092
Then a man stood up and raised his hands.

14
00:00:48.093 --> 00:00:51.538
"Time for a story!" he shouted.

15
00:00:51.539 --> 00:00:54.158
The crowd cheered.

16
00:00:54.159 --> 00:01:00.035
"We are happy to have Duman the storyteller with us!" the man said.

17
00:01:00.036 --> 00:01:02.270
Everyone clapped.

18
00:01:02.271 --> 00:01:08.278
Then, a man wearing a colorful robe stood up in the middle of the shop.

19
00:01:08.279 --> 00:01:14.351
It was Duman the storyteller, and he began to speak.

20
00:01:14.352 --> 00:01:17.476
"Prince Babar wanted to see the world.

21
00:01:17.477 --> 00:01:21.167
His father, the sultan, would not allow him to go.

22
00:01:21.168 --> 00:01:25.139
The sultan wanted the prince to stay in the palace and marry.

23
00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:31.566
‘But Father,’ said the prince, ‘I must see our great empire before I marry.’"

24
00:01:31.567 --> 00:01:35.071
Duman pulled out a bright handkerchief.

25
00:01:35.072 --> 00:01:37.979
He waved it in front of his face.

26
00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:40.601
Then his voice changed.

27
00:01:40.602 --> 00:01:44.626
"‘You can see the empire after you marry!’

28
00:01:44.627 --> 00:01:48.231
At that moment, the prince’s mother came in."

29
00:01:48.232 --> 00:01:51.456
Duman waved the handkerchief again.

30
00:01:51.457 --> 00:01:55.741
This time his voice was high, like a woman’s.

31
00:01:55.742 --> 00:01:59.941
"‘Babar! I’ve found the perfect bride for you.

32
00:01:59.942 --> 00:02:06.358
She looks exactly like me.’"

33
00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:10.633
All the men in the coffee shop laughed loudly.

34
00:02:10.634 --> 00:02:17.021
"He’s doing all the characters himself!" giggled Mandy.

35
00:02:17.022 --> 00:02:21.803
Berk stopped talking with Hasad and stood next to Vinnie.

36
00:02:21.804 --> 00:02:24.264
"Isn’t he funny?"

37
00:02:24.264 --> 00:02:27.293
Vinnie pointed to the storyteller.

38
00:02:27.294 --> 00:02:31.476
Berk smiled, but then suddenly froze.

39
00:02:31.477 --> 00:02:35.092
In fact, everyone stopped laughing.

40
00:02:35.093 --> 00:02:38.812
A group of men wearing uniforms walked in.

41
00:02:38.813 --> 00:02:42.535
They had long swords in their belts.

42
00:02:42.536 --> 00:02:46.208
"We want coffee," demanded one of them.

43
00:02:46.209 --> 00:02:51.681
"You," he said to the storyteller, "Go on with your story."

44
00:02:51.682 --> 00:02:55.335
Duman nervously continued.

45
00:02:55.336 --> 00:02:59.000
"Who are they?" Vinnie asked Berk.

46
00:02:59.001 --> 00:03:02.809
"The Janissary," explained Berk.

47
00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:06.447
"They used to be slaves from outside the empire.

48
00:03:06.448 --> 00:03:09.201
They’re trained to be the best fighters.

49
00:03:09.202 --> 00:03:12.503
The Janissary protect the sultan."

50
00:03:12.504 --> 00:03:17.969
"You, children! Come over here!" one guard shouted.

51
00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:21.007
The children walked over to him.

52
00:03:21.008 --> 00:03:23.829
"Who are you?" he asked.

53
00:03:23.830 --> 00:03:29.082
"Our caravan just arrived in Istanbul and . . . " began Berk.

54
00:03:29.083 --> 00:03:33.352
The guard grabbed Berk’s bag and looked inside.

55
00:03:33.353 --> 00:03:37.092
"This bag is full of silver!" he said.

56
00:03:37.093 --> 00:03:40.772
"Young thieves were seen in the palace this morning."

57
00:03:40.773 --> 00:03:42.637
"I wasn’t with them, sir.

58
00:03:42.638 --> 00:03:47.270
That silver is for my father," Berk explained.

59
00:03:47.271 --> 00:03:53.016
"And what do you have in your pockets?" another soldier asked the children.

60
00:03:53.017 --> 00:03:56.737
Berk and Vinnie had nothing in their pockets.

61
00:03:56.738 --> 00:03:58.867
But Mandy did.

62
00:03:58.868 --> 00:04:02.746
She pulled out her mother’s glittering earrings.

63
00:04:02.747 --> 00:04:05.039
Berk looked at her in shock.

64
00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:07.267
So did the soldiers.

65
00:04:07.268 --> 00:04:10.466
The soldier took the earrings from Mandy.

66
00:04:10.467 --> 00:04:14.208
He held them in his palm and stared at them.

67
00:04:14.209 --> 00:04:24.178
"This jewelry surely does not belong to a little girl!" the soldier said.

